  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nUpper level ridging builds into the region through Saturday.\nWarmer and drier conditions are forecast as a result. Expect high\ntemperatures in the 50s and 60s today before warming further into\nthe 70s on Saturday. Models have been consistently showing breezy\nwinds coming out of the Bighorn Basin today, bringing gusts in the\n30s and 40s mph south of Billings to the MT/WY border.\n\nA dry cold front will move through the area Saturday evening,\nbringing high temperatures down into the 50s and 60s for Sunday. \nThe latest forecast has temperatures in the 60s to low 70s for the\nfirst half of the week.\n\nDepending on the track of a low off the west coast middle of next\nweek, the region could get into a pattern of daily afternoon \nshowers and a few thunderstorms. Currently there are low chances \nfor precipitation across south- central MT Tuesday into Wednesday.\nThere is still uncertainty at this time, so watch the forecast to\nsee how this system progresses. TS/PM",
